<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Hans Egede</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1686–1758</span> · <a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Hans Egede was a Norwegian Lutheran missionary who sailed to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/greenland">Greenland</a> in 1721 hoping to find the descendants of the medieval Norse settlers. Finding only <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/inuit">Inuit</a>, he founded a mission and trading post at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nuuk">Godthåb</a> (Nuuk) in 1728 and learned their language. His work began Danish-Norwegian colonisation of Greenland, and he is known as the Apostle of Greenland.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/hans-egede.jpg" alt="Hans Egede" width="320" height="417" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Johan Hörner · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Hans_Poulsen_Egede.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
